{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS3iBbo22Sbbjco7SSc8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Я уже поменял структуру system-промпта. Сейчас сделаю так, чтобы system собирался один раз за reply, и допишу ANSWER.md."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1145,"cache_read_input_tokens":29434,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1145},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"613961a4-3c91-4dbf-b10c-373eb36600c4","uuid":"c30ea458-9550-472a-9939-850f89c4f85a","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:40:18.667Z","request_id":"req_011CgS3iB8Wf8fN3uXwTi9KS"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS3iBbo22Sbbjco7SSc8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01P2izhU4boRSAqG6MkaCVhF","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'E'\ns=open('bot.py').read()\ns=s.replace('def build_request(a, messages, tools, today):\\n    return {\"model\": MODEL, \"max_tokens\": MAX_TOKENS, \"system\": build_system(a, today), \"tools\": tools, \"messages\": messages}',\n'def build_request(system, messages, tools):\\n    return {\"model\": MODEL, \"max_tokens\": MAX_TOKENS, \"system\": system, \"tools\": tools, \"messages\": messages}')\ns=s.replace('    tools = select_tools(text)\\n','    tools = select_tools(text)\\n    system = build_system(a, today)  # built once: a save_fact mid-loop must not change the cached prefix\\n')\ns=s.replace('build_request(a, messages, tools, today)','build_request(system, messages, tools)')\nopen('bot.py','w').write(s)\nE\npython3 -c \"\nimport bot,datetime as dt\na=bot.load_athlete('42');print(bot.build_system(a,dt.date.today()))\" | head -c 300\ncat > ANSWER.md <<'E'\n# Fix: save_fact no longer invalidates the whole system prompt cache\n\n## Cause\n`build_system` put instructions, profile and facts into ONE text block with ONE\n`cache_control`. A cache hit needs an identical prefix, so any new fact changed the block\nand the whole prompt (~1000 tokens) was re-written at full price. The system prompt was\nalso rebuilt on every tool round, so round 2 after `save_fact` always missed (see the\n`cache_creation_input_tokens ~1000` rows in logs/usage.jsonl).\n\n## Changes (bot.py)\n- `athlete_context` split into `athlete_profile` (name, zones, goal, language: rarely\n  changes) and `athlete_memory` (today's date + facts: the volatile part).\n- `build_system` returns two blocks, ordered stable -> volatile:\n  1. INSTRUCTIONS + profile, with a cache breakpoint;\n  2. date + facts, with its own breakpoint.\n  A new fact now only invalidates block 2. The date also moved there, so the daily date change no longer busts the instructions.\n- `reply()` builds the system prompt once per message and passes it to `build_request`,\n  so a `save_fact` inside the tool loop does not change the prefix between rounds.\n\n## Caveats (not verified: no API access here, nothing was run against the API)\n- Minimum cacheable prefix on Sonnet 4.5 is 1024 tokens. From the log, tools + instructions\n  are ~950 tokens by my estimate; with the profile (~70) the first breakpoint sits right at\n  ~1020. If it falls below 1024 it is silently not cached and the savings disappear.\n  Check logs/usage.jsonl after deploying: `cache_read_input_tokens` should stay > 0 on the\n  call after a `save_fact`. If not, add a little static content (e.g. a few examples) to block 1.\n- Tools come BEFORE system in the cache prefix. The keyword-based tool selection\n  (plan_week / predict_race) changes the tool list between messages and busts the cache\n  too (the 1305/1334 creation rows). I left it alone as NOTES.md asks; a fix would be\n  to always send all tools (with a breakpoint on the last one), at the cost of the token saving.\nE"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1145,"cache_read_input_tokens":29434,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1145},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"613961a4-3c91-4dbf-b10c-373eb36600c4","uuid":"7a0dd98a-bd80-46f7-8162-b73e3139de42","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:40:25.796Z","request_id":"req_011CgS3iB8Wf8fN3uXwTi9KS","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01P2izhU4boRSAqG6MkaCVhF":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/h-7ENfvI && python3 - <<'E'\ns=open('bot.py').read()\ns=s.replace('def build_request(a, messages, tools, today):\\n    return {\"model\": MODEL, \"max_tokens\": MAX_TOKENS, \"system\": build_system(a, today), \"tools\": tools, \"messages\": messages}',\n'def build_request(system, messages, tools):\\n    return {\"model\": MODEL, \"max_tokens\": MAX_TOKENS, \"system\": system, \"tools\": tools, \"messages\": messages}')\ns=s.replace('    tools = select_tools(text)\\n','    tools = select_tools(text)\\n    system = build_system(a, today)  # built once: a save_fact mid-loop must not change the cached prefix\\n')\ns=s.replace('build_request(a, messages, tools, today)','build_request(system, messages, tools)')\nopen('bot.py','w').write(s)\nE\npython3 -c \"\nimport bot,datetime as dt\na=bot.load_athlete('42');print(bot.build_system(a,dt.date.today()))\" | head -c 300\ncat > ANSWER.md <<'E'\n# Fix: save_fact no longer invalidates the whole system prompt cache\n\n## Cause\n`build_system` put instructions, profile and facts into ONE text block with ONE\n`cache_control`. A cache hit needs an identical prefix, so any new fact changed the block\nand the whole prompt (~1000 tokens) was re-written at full price. The system prompt was\nalso rebuilt on every tool round, so round 2 after `save_fact` always missed (see the\n`cache_creation_input_tokens ~1000` rows in logs/usage.jsonl).\n\n## Changes (bot.py)\n- `athlete_context` split into `athlete_profile` (name, zones, goal, language: rarely\n  changes) and `athlete_memory` (today's date + facts: the volatile part).\n- `build_system` returns two blocks, ordered stable -> volatile:\n  1. INSTRUCTIONS + profile, with a cache breakpoint;\n  2. date + facts, with its own breakpoint.\n  A new fact now only invalidates block 2. The date also moved there, so the daily date change no longer busts the instructions.\n- `reply()` builds the system prompt once per message and passes it to `build_request`,\n  so a `save_fact` inside the tool loop does not change the prefix between rounds.\n\n## Caveats (not verified: no API access here, nothing was run against the API)\n- Minimum cacheable prefix on Sonnet 4.5 is 1024 tokens. From the log, tools + instructions\n  are ~950 tokens by my estimate; with the profile (~70) the first breakpoint sits right at\n  ~1020. If it falls below 1024 it is silently not cached and the savings disappear.\n  Check logs/usage.jsonl after deploying: `cache_read_input_tokens` should stay > 0 on the\n  call after a `save_fact`. If not, add a little static content (e.g. a few examples) to block 1.\n- Tools come BEFORE system in the cache prefix. The keyword-based tool selection\n  (plan_week / predict_race) changes the tool list between messages and busts the cache\n  too (the 1305/1334 creation rows). I left it alone as NOTES.md asks; a fix would be\n  to always send all tools (with a breakpoint on the last one), at the cost of the token saving.\nE"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01P2izhU4boRSAqG6MkaCVhF":{"cwd":"/private/tmp/h-7ENfvI"}}}
